        "type": "dialogue",
        "legend": "M: Mike  A: Alice",
        "turns": [
          {
            "speaker": "M",
            "content": [
              { "t": "text", "v": "So here’s the question for our discussion: In what ways are " },
              { "t": "gloss", "v": "Mars", "zh": "火星" },
              { "t": "text", "v": " and Earth " },
              { "t": "vocab", "v": "similar", "ref": "v-similar" },
              { "t": "text", "v": "? Can you think of any, Alice?" }
            ]
          },
          {
            "speaker": "A",
            "content": [
              { "t": "text", "v": "I’m not sure. Do both planets have the right " },
              { "t": "vocab", "v": "temperature", "ref": "v-temperature" },
              { "t": "text", "v": " for life?" }
            ]
          },
          {
            "speaker": "M",
            "content": [
              { "t": "text", "v": "I don’t think so. Mars is much colder. It’s about minus 55 " },
              { "t": "gloss", "v": "degrees Celsius", "zh": "摄氏度" },
              { "t": "text", "v": " most of the time." }
            ]
          },
          {
            "speaker": "A",
            "content": [
              { "t": "text", "v": "Well, then, are the two planets about the same " },
              { "t": "vocab", "v": "distance", "ref": "v-distance" },
              { "t": "text", "v": " from the Sun?" }
            ]
          },
          {
            "speaker": "M",
            "content": [
              { "t": "text", "v": "No way! Earth is about 150 million kilometers away from the Sun. The distance from Mars to the Sun is about 228 million kilometers." }
            ]
          },
          {
            "speaker": "A",
            "content": [
              { "t": "text", "v": "Yes, but in space that’s not that far. " },
              { "t": "gloss", "v": "Jupiter", "zh": "木星" },
              { "t": "text", "v": ", for example, is nearly 780 million kilometers from the Sun. That’s why we use " },
              { "t": "gloss", "v": "astronomical units", "zh": "天文单位" },
              { "t": "text", "v": " when we talk about distances in space. Earth is 1 astronomical unit from the Sun, and Mars is 1.5. The difference doesn’t sound so big when you look at it that way." }
            ]
          },
          {
            "speaker": "M",
            "content": [
              { "t": "text", "v": "I see what you mean. Jupiter is 5.2 astronomical units from the Sun, so I guess you’re right." }
            ]
          },
          {
            "speaker": "A",
            "content": [
              { "t": "text", "v": "I also found another point. The days on both planets are almost the same " },
              { "t": "gloss", "v": "length", "zh": "时长" },
              { "t": "text", "v": ". Earth’s day is 24 hours long, and Mars’ is only about half an hour longer." }
            ]
          },
          {
            "speaker": "M",
            "content": [
              { "t": "text", "v": "Yes. Besides that, they both have water. Mars may have had huge oceans in the past, but most of the water there is probably frozen now." }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
